{"version":3,"kind":"Article","sha256":"c3facb068b99508df5c57f689e4192701df2653c1655ff34cb7d35a57c94bb56","slug":"index","location":"/intro.md","dependencies":[],"frontmatter":{"title":"From Models to Learning","content_includes_title":false,"authors":[{"nameParsed":{"literal":"Pierre-Luc Bacon","given":"Pierre-Luc","family":"Bacon"},"name":"Pierre-Luc Bacon","id":"contributors-myst-generated-uid-0"}],"github":"https://github.com/pierrelux/rlbook","math":{"\\Proj":{"macro":"\\mathsf{P}"},"\\Residual":{"macro":"\\mathsf{N}"},"\\Contraction":{"macro":"\\mathsf{T}"},"\\Bellman":{"macro":"\\mathsf{L}"},"\\BellmanPi":{"macro":"\\mathsf{L}_\\pi"},"\\BellmanQuad":{"macro":"\\widetilde{\\mathsf{L}}"},"\\EulerResidual":{"macro":"\\mathsf{H}"},"\\Policy":{"macro":"\\pi"}},"source_url":"https://github.com/pierrelux/rlbook/blob/main/intro.md","edit_url":"https://github.com/pierrelux/rlbook/edit/main/intro.md","exports":[{"format":"md","filename":"intro.md","url":"/rlbook/build/intro-5358f4449f5db4f73ac9c3b3d320036e.md"}]},"mdast":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"block","children":[{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":8,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"On the TCV tokamak, a learned policy controlled plasma by issuing voltage\ncommands to 19 magnetic coils at 10 kHz ","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"key":"i6y5Qt5r7C"},{"type":"citeGroup","kind":"parenthetical","children":[{"type":"cite","kind":"parenthetical","label":"Degrave2022","identifier":"degrave2022","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Degrave ","key":"Msi9iXhVXu"},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"et al.","key":"tZZwRp49f0"}],"key":"jR1l2XccPO"},{"type":"text","value":", 2022","key":"i29eXSnMpV"}],"enumerator":"1","key":"tDZxp3kQKz"}],"key":"JXW099NFTp"},{"type":"text","value":". The policy did\nnot form the plasma, choose the sensors, define a safe operating region, or\ndecide what a voltage command meant. Conventional control first formed and\nstabilized the plasma, and a simulator specified the physical and operational\nconditions under which the policy was trained.","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"key":"TidW3Sq5cQ"}],"key":"MbcJBFxKlO"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":10,"column":1},"end":{"line":13,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"The learning algorithm therefore operated inside a decision problem that had\nalready been formulated. The system boundary, state and observations, available\nactions, objective, and termination conditions were fixed before training.\nThese choices determine what a learned policy can observe, cause, and optimize.","position":{"start":{"line":10,"column":1},"end":{"line":10,"column":1}},"key":"rT1MJZ9FVO"}],"key":"VNY54oTsIh"},{"type":"admonition","children":[{"type":"admonitionTitle","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Working definition","position":{"start":{"line":15,"column":1},"end":{"line":15,"column":1}},"key":"SaOF6A1wjU"}],"key":"fFZSg1CqPF"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":18,"column":1},"end":{"line":21,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":18,"column":1},"end":{"line":18,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Reinforcement learning","position":{"start":{"line":18,"column":1},"end":{"line":18,"column":1}},"key":"OgVDkNYIaA"}],"key":"KB06ubYJqR"},{"type":"text","value":" studies how data from interaction or recorded\nexperience can be used to evaluate and improve decisions whose consequences\nunfold through a dynamical system. Present actions affect future states and\ntherefore future opportunities and outcomes.","position":{"start":{"line":18,"column":1},"end":{"line":18,"column":1}},"key":"O0IfdmTOLQ"}],"key":"gL4yr3AvMx"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":23,"column":1},"end":{"line":26,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"This is a problem class rather than a single algorithm. Temporal-difference,\nvalue-based, and policy-gradient methods are solution families. The state,\naction set, objective, constraints, and transition interface define the problem\nthey are asked to solve.","position":{"start":{"line":23,"column":1},"end":{"line":23,"column":1}},"key":"EQdgFJoWXo"}],"key":"zyFoO5Ypoq"}],"class":"course-definition","key":"TNd0LjBsLz"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":29,"column":1},"end":{"line":34,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Sequential decision-making is the broader subject. Trajectory optimization,\nfeedback control, and exact dynamic programming can solve some sequential\nproblems without learning from data. Reinforcement learning enters when a model,\nvalue function, or policy must be estimated from samples or interaction. The\nbook develops the common mathematical structure before introducing the places\nwhere models, values, or policies must be estimated from data.","position":{"start":{"line":29,"column":1},"end":{"line":29,"column":1}},"key":"al3jYwompq"}],"key":"TNjwVyi2XP"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":36,"column":1},"end":{"line":41,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"An application does not arrive with this interface attached. Its formulation\nmust specify where the system ends, what is known when an action is chosen,\nwhich interventions are physically possible, how outcomes are valued, and\nwhich requirements cannot be traded against reward. An optimizer can use only\nthe variables, objectives, and constraints in that formulation. An omitted\nrequirement cannot affect its solution.","position":{"start":{"line":36,"column":1},"end":{"line":36,"column":1}},"key":"fCIaDwWn4q"}],"key":"DmDc4uNlSw"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"position":{"start":{"line":43,"column":1},"end":{"line":43,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"The Agent-Environment Interface","position":{"start":{"line":43,"column":1},"end":{"line":43,"column":1}},"key":"AobDDcL9BS"}],"identifier":"the-agent-environment-interface","label":"The Agent-Environment Interface","html_id":"the-agent-environment-interface","implicit":true,"key":"S3xpZsCIwa"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":45,"column":1},"end":{"line":49,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"The standard agent-environment loop begins after a state signal, actions, and\nrewards have been selected. ","position":{"start":{"line":45,"column":1},"end":{"line":45,"column":1}},"key":"JzlCNN89uh"},{"type":"citeGroup","kind":"narrative","children":[{"type":"cite","kind":"narrative","label":"SuttonBarto2018","identifier":"suttonbarto2018","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Sutton & Barto (2018)","key":"rlSozY5OVU"}],"enumerator":"2","key":"awnbuwr4uo"}],"key":"ZXls9KIkBU"},{"type":"text","value":" treat the state signal as\nthe output of a preprocessing system and set aside much of its construction in\norder to study decision making. Their abstraction isolates the learning\nproblem; it does not make the preceding formulation choices disappear.","position":{"start":{"line":45,"column":1},"end":{"line":45,"column":1}},"key":"SuE7GFXmrk"}],"key":"JXOw5oWXuz"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":51,"column":1},"end":{"line":53,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"The familiar agent-environment loop also appears in other fields. Control\ntheory, operations research, and econometrics use different names for related\ncausal exchanges and ask different questions of them.","position":{"start":{"line":51,"column":1},"end":{"line":51,"column":1}},"key":"y07sQkPQJY"}],"key":"qIRWQv6y6X"},{"type":"div","identifier":"fig-interaction-loop-vocabularies","label":"fig-interaction-loop-vocabularies","class":"interaction-lenses-figure","children":[{"type":"div","class":"interaction-lenses","children":[{"type":"div","class":"interaction-lens","children":[{"type":"div","class":"interaction-lens-title","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Reinforcement learning","key":"ggBreMYOLJ"}],"key":"uKF9lBBUqV"},{"type":"div","class":"interaction-loop","children":[{"type":"div","class":"interaction-node","children":[{"type":"span","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Agent","key":"Ce8HqIlBLO"}],"key":"YlhmiSuqSJ"},{"type":"text","value":" ","key":"L0yp1LEn3a"},{"type":"span","class":"interaction-node-subtitle","children":[{"type":"text","value":"policy ","key":"sQkDDnjGX7"},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"π","key":"zyJEfpteQw"}],"key":"vpGU4RYHkp"}],"key":"mLZpsvF2FC"}],"key":"qklMLxe6u1"},{"type":"div","class":"interaction-arrows","children":[{"type":"span","children":[{"type":"text","value":"action ","key":"k3v4XFWJaZ"},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A","key":"wx72sbjszI"}],"key":"ynMoy8Uluc"},{"type":"subscript","children":[{"type":"text","value":"t","key":"bxuZN2aIiE"}],"key":"OlT5tizA5D"}],"key":"jah4Z6B4XV"},{"type":"div","class":"interaction-arrow-glyph","children":[{"type":"span","children":[{"type":"text","value":"→","key":"FYEL6p71D0"}],"key":"hDuWRmcFSn"},{"type":"span","children":[{"type":"text","value":"←","key":"XBmdpqX9ab"}],"key":"sxQwoGh9Yo"}],"key":"mfQnGJuwpa"},{"type":"span","children":[{"type":"text","value":"state ","key":"MJFt9RmHgf"},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"S","key":"kxtGqeUPT5"}],"key":"h80Hojs32f"},{"type":"subscript","children":[{"type":"text","value":"t+1","key":"FLctDAfnIt"}],"key":"IyzjnEzo1d"},{"type":"break","key":"DNpFBtRZvH"},{"type":"text","value":"reward ","key":"h60XITHzft"},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"R","key":"zn1jMNNlac"}],"key":"T5Zd7i29C8"},{"type":"subscript","children":[{"type":"text","value":"t+1","key":"z1G4aBsS3L"}],"key":"TlZyFLaGG1"}],"key":"rkmFFOg6c5"}],"key":"Fo6QYF4g8m"},{"type":"div","class":"interaction-node interaction-node-world","children":[{"type":"span","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Environment","key":"NI1TBvfV6b"}],"key":"mN0HfQg3nK"},{"type":"text","value":" ","ke